Airsyntax

Airsyntax is a self-contained desktop application engineered to integrate an asynchronous ASGI server lifecycle directly alongside a native operating system window manager.

Key Features

Bilingual Support: Available in dedicated English (server_en) and Chinese (server_zh) interface implementations tailored for localized workflow integration.

Instant QR Provisioning: Automatically generates and renders dynamic session QR codes upon tunnel activation, allowing immediate scanning and connection from iPhones.

Bi-Directional Real-Time Relay:

Desktop-to-iPhone: Broadcast text payloads, notes, or formatted strings instantly to all connected iPhones.

iPhone-to-Desktop: Push captured or edited text directly back from mobile clients to the host computer interface with automated clipboard synchronization.

Zero System Footprint: Operates entirely as a portable standalone executable requiring no manual network configuration or background service installation on target machines.

How It Works: 

Airsyntax functions as a parent application that embeds a high-performance Python ASGI backend directly inside a native window container. Upon startup, it boots an asynchronous Uvicorn/FastAPI server alongside a dynamic tunneling engine to securely expose local socket instances, while PyWebView renders a clean, frameless interface for seamless cross-device communication.

Installation
Prerequisites

Windows 10 / 11 (64-bit) or compatible desktop environment supporting Python/PyWebView runtimes.

Getting Started

Go to the Releases page.

Download the latest release build (Airsyntax-v1.0.0.zip or installer executable).

Extract and launch Airsyntax.exe.

Quick Start Guide

Launch Airsyntax: Open the standalone desktop application.

Initialize Tunnel: Wait for the initialization sequence to complete and the dynamic connection tunnel to establish.

Scan QR Code: Scan the generated session QR code using your iPhone camera to open the secure mobile relay interface.

Broadcast & Sync: Push payloads instantly from the desktop interface or sync text back from your mobile client with automated clipboard integration.

Tech Stack & Architecture

Server Runtime: Python, Uvicorn, FastAPI (high-throughput asynchronous routing and WebSockets).

Desktop Interface: PyWebView for a frameless, flicker-free native window container.

Communication Protocol: WebSockets (/ws, /admin-ws) and HTTP JSON API for real-time bi-directional message dispatching.

Tunneling & Scaling: Secure dynamic tunnel routing supporting concurrent multi-client connections from unlimited mobile devices.

Security & Privacy

Zero Cloud Intermediary: Airsyntax operates locally on your machine, establishing direct communication streams between your host application and connected mobile clients.

Local Data Encapsulation: Session states, active socket tunnels, and broadcast buffers remain securely handled within local execution boundaries.

